{{- if .Role}}
## Your role: {{.Role.Name}}

This task is split across several worktrees, one per role. You own the **{{.Role.Name}}** part of it and nothing else.
{{if .Role.Integrates}}
You are the integrating role. The other roles work on their own branches off `{{.Role.Trunk}}` and merge back into it. This worktree is the trunk checkout, and it is the only one that opens a PR.
{{- else}}
Your branch merges into `{{.Role.Trunk}}`. Do not open a PR: the integrating role does that once every role has merged.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Role.Siblings}}

Worked in parallel right now, so not yours to touch: {{join .Role.Siblings " · "}}.
{{- end}}

{{end}}
## This worktree

- Forked from `{{.Base}}` — diff your work with `git diff {{.Base}}...HEAD`.
{{- if and .Role (not .Role.Integrates)}}
- Merges into `{{.Role.Trunk}}`, not into `{{.PRBase | default .Base}}`.
{{- end}}
{{- if and .PRBase (ne .PRBase .Base)}}
- Branches from `{{.Base}}`, but PRs target `{{.PRBase}}`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Setup}}
- Setup: run `{{.Setup}}`.
{{- end}}
{{- if .Verify}}
- Before done: {{join .Verify " · "}}
{{- end}}
- Keep a `.state.md` at the root with at least a `next:` line (the one action to resume with). Update it as you work. norn surfaces it on the dashboard, and it's git-ignored so it never lands in a commit.
- Disposable — clean up with `norn --clean` once it's merged.
